Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:46:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 362/638] [AROS] Carry Mojo packets over Exec MessagePorts

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: duplex-messageport-transport-runtime-pass
ROOT_CAUSE: AROS Mojo endpoints had transferable identity but no byte or handle transport; ChannelPosix cannot operate on task-owned Exec MsgPorts.
FIX_REASON: Add MEMF_PUBLIC packets, per-side pending queues, task-owned receive ports, transferable platform handles, explicit stop/peer-close packets, and a focused hosted probe.
SCOPE: mojo/public/cpp/platform/BUILD.gn; mojo/public/cpp/platform/aros_channel.{cc,h}; mojo/public/cpp/platform/aros_channel_probe.cc
VALIDATION: Focused target linked at -j32; hosted 16 GiB run reported PASS queued=1 duplex=1 handles=1 peer_close=1 and exited in 4.80 seconds.
RISK: The spin lock is intentionally minimal for bring-up; full Mojo invitation and browser/renderer traffic remain the next gates.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: transferable endpoint identity -> task-owned MsgPorts -> early-send queue -> attached-handle transfer -> peer-close semantics -> focused hosted PASS.
Evidence:-channel-aros-20260728
